# The shortcut's store: readings come back as Readings, but outages come back as the lines they are kept as, and a
# summary is kept and given back as a line; the Outage that `saveOutage` puts no get gives back, and no Summary type
# exists. `summary` returns the kept line when there is one (`if (kept) return kept`), else reads the day's readings and
# writes the new line: the code after the early return is the other arm of that choice. A library's operation whose
# result the body names (`readFileSync`, `find`, `map`) is a step; what it touches stays its caller's. Each file is
# read, used and written by the route: it stands on both sides.
#
# #new: new-A a parameter at the own arrow by its type, new-B an own arrow taking every class its steps build, new-C an
# unnamed call in a chain a step, new-F a class's read-and-written place between, new-G an own arrow dropping a value
# it uses and hands on, new-L the code after an early return no arm.

route shortcut.store.ReadingStore
step ReadingStore()/ReadingStore()
step ReadingStore()/ReadingStore.save
step ReadingStore()/ReadingStore.history
step ReadingStore()/ReadingStore.history/Reading()
step ReadingStore()/ReadingStore.saveOutage
step ReadingStore()/ReadingStore.outages
step ReadingStore()/ReadingStore.summary
step ReadingStore()/ReadingStore.summary/readFileSync
step ReadingStore()/ReadingStore.summary/find
